  "id": "constructive-thinking",
  "term": "constructive thinking",
  "definition": "Constructive thinking is a pattern of automatic habitual thoughts, both helpful and unhelpful, that influences how well a person approaches problems in a solution-focused way. Strong constructive thinking is linked with adaptive beliefs, better emotion management, and action-oriented coping, whereas weak constructive thinking involves maladaptive automatic ideas that can interfere with monitoring emotions.",
